### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5090

### 1. Create room
# @name createRoom
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Study room 1",
  "capacity": 10
}

###
@roomId = {{createRoom.response.body.$.id}}

### 2. Get room
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}

### 3. Get a missing room (expected: 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### 4. Create booking (change the dates to the future!)
# @name createBooking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

###
@bookingId = {{createBooking.response.body.$.id}}

### 5. Get booking
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}

### 6. Overlapping booking (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "bogdan",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T11:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T13:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 7. Cancel booking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel

### 8. Requests for the rules in ASSIGNMENT.md

### R1: empty name (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "  ", "capacity": 10 }

### R1: capacity 0 (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Room X", "capacity": 0 }

### Booking for a missing room (expected: 404, before validation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "", "startUtc": "2030-01-10T10:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-01-10T09:00:00Z", "attendees": 0 }

### R2: bookedBy missing (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": " ", "startUtc": "2030-02-01T10:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-02-01T11:00:00Z", "attendees": 2 }

### R3: end equal to start (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "ana", "startUtc": "2030-02-01T10:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-02-01T10:00:00Z", "attendees": 2 }

### R4: attendees above capacity (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "ana", "startUtc": "2030-02-01T10:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-02-01T11:00:00Z", "attendees": 11 }

### R5: start in the past (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "ana", "startUtc": "2020-02-01T10:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2020-02-01T11:00:00Z", "attendees": 2 }

### R6: 4h 1m (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "ana", "startUtc": "2030-02-01T10:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-02-01T14:01:00Z", "attendees": 2 }

### R6: exactly 4h (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "ana", "startUtc": "2030-03-01T10:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-03-01T14:00:00Z", "attendees": 2 }

### R7: touching the previous booking (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "bogdan", "startUtc": "2030-03-01T14:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-03-01T15:00:00Z", "attendees": 2 }

### R8: cancel again (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel

### R8: cancel a missing booking (expected: 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/cancel

### R8: the cancelled interval is free again (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "bogdan", "startUtc": "2030-01-10T11:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-01-10T13:00:00Z", "attendees": 4 }

### R9: second room, to show the limit is across all rooms
# @name createRoom2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Study room 2", "capacity": 10 }

###
@roomId2 = {{createRoom2.response.body.$.id}}

### R9: maria, 1st booking of the day, room 1 (expected: 201)
# @name maria1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "maria", "startUtc": "2030-05-01T08:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-05-01T09:00:00Z", "attendees": 2 }

###
@maria1Id = {{maria1.response.body.$.id}}

### R9: maria, 2nd booking of the day, room 2 (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId2}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "maria", "startUtc": "2030-05-01T10:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-05-01T11:00:00Z", "attendees": 2 }

### R9: maria, 3rd booking of the same day (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId2}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "maria", "startUtc": "2030-05-01T15:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-05-01T16:00:00Z", "attendees": 2 }

### R9: maria, booking on another day (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId2}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "maria", "startUtc": "2030-05-02T15:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-05-02T16:00:00Z", "attendees": 2 }

### R9: cancel maria's 1st booking (expected: 204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{maria1Id}}/cancel

### R9: the 3rd booking now passes, cancelled ones do not count (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId2}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "maria", "startUtc": "2030-05-01T15:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-05-01T16:00:00Z", "attendees": 2 }

### R10: large room (capacity 20)
# @name bigRoom
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Big room", "capacity": 20 }

###
@bigRoomId = {{bigRoom.response.body.$.id}}

### R10: large room, 2h 1m (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{bigRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "ion", "startUtc": "2030-06-01T10:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-06-01T12:01:00Z", "attendees": 5 }

### R10: large room, exactly 2h (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{bigRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "ion", "startUtc": "2030-06-01T10:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-06-01T12:00:00Z", "attendees": 5 }

### R10: room with capacity 10 keeps 4h (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "ion", "startUtc": "2030-06-01T10:00:00Z", "endUtc": "2030-06-01T13:00:00Z", "attendees": 5 }

### R11: booking that starts in less than 60 minutes.
# Change startUtc to about 30 minutes from now (UTC) before running, endUtc 1 hour after it.
# @name soonBooking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookedBy": "dan", "startUtc": "2026-11-19T08:30:00Z", "endUtc": "2026-11-19T09:30:00Z", "attendees": 2 }

###
@soonBookingId = {{soonBooking.response.body.$.id}}

### R11: cancel less than 60 minutes before the start (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{soonBookingId}}/cancel
